From aeaa5af4381023ee4cb3bb28a076bb0d36b9aed8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Somalapuram Amaranath <somalapuram@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 10:06:25 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] drm_hwcomposer: DIAGNOSTIC logging for client composition
 and modifiers

Temporary instrumentation for the pc_x86_64 port. Two questions the device
currently answers with silence:

  1. Every layer reports CLIENT and nothing says which of the four conditions
     in IsClientLayer() is responsible.
  2. Enabling tiled allocation produced a garbled panel while screencap stayed
     perfect, and no modifier value is ever logged.

Three probes, each self-throttling so none can flood at frame rate:

  CLIENT-REASON     GenericCompositionPlanner::IsClientLayer, once per distinct
                    cause (atomic bitmask), naming sf_type / no_fb / ctm_by_gpu
                    / forced_scaling, plus a one-shot line if any layer IS
                    device-capable.
  TEST-COMMIT-FAIL  DrmAtomicStateManager, test-only path. This was ALOGV, i.e.
                    compiled out of a release build, so a failing plane test
                    left no trace whatsoever.
  FB-IMPORT         DrmFbImporter, once per distinct format/modifier pair. This
                    is the only place bo->modifiers[0] decides between
                    drmModeAddFB2() and drmModeAddFB2WithModifiers().

Revert once the cause is understood.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GbE6Dti9ffdUvhbzRyp3g4
